;; env.bl — omega's project file, read by the `bl` launcher (~/.local/bin/bl).
;;
;; `:bl` pins the beam-lisp build omega runs on. A pinned commit is built ONCE,
;; clean, in a detached tree (~/.cache/bl/build-trees/<sha>) and kept in the
;; store, so omega neither rebuilds nor breaks when the beam-lisp main checkout
;; carries uncommitted work (whose stale boot tier made every run recompile for
;; minutes). Supersedes PLAN-001 D12 ("always the latest checkout").
;;
;; 94700545 (2026-10-04): beam-lisp main after the bl-js-actors merge — brings
;; bl.doc.spans, system.place and js.eval, which the vendored bl-ed and the UX
;; slice need (FEAT-001's re-pin). On it: omega's suite 16/16 files green;
;; headless 8/9 — `live-model-streams-into-the-window` asserts the word
;; "writing" vanishes, which a real model's answer about write-ahead logs can
;; contain (passed 2/2 on re-run; content-dependent, not a pin regression).
;; Previous: 2360b32e.
;;
;; To move: pick a beam-lisp commit, run `bin/bl test` and `bin/omega-headless`
;; with BL_USE=commit:<sha>, then change the pin. To run the LIVE checkout
;; instead, once: OMEGA_BL=~/code/undefine/beam-lisp/bin/bl bin/…
{:name "omega"
 :paths ["src"]
 :bl "commit:94700545"}
